{
	"_description": "Reference vectors of the analyser scorers (_shared/ui/layout_analysis/analyser_scores.js, gate tools/test/test-analyser-scores.cjs): a layout, a text or corpus, a keyboard and the value the analyser gives. « basis » says where the value comes from: « tool » = printed by the analyser's own code, run on the same input; « published » = a table the analyser's author published; « hand » = computed by hand from the formula of docs/design/analyser-scores.md. A text with « keep_line_breaks » is counted with its line breaks in the main tables; any other text is counted by the engine (ngramsFromText), whose break tables give KLA and KLAnext their Enter and Tab presses. KLAnext's values are its site's, printed to 2 decimals. Fixtures: analysers/kla_alice_ch1.txt is KLA's preset (Lewis Carroll, public domain; KLA is MIT), analysers/ergol_*.json are the Ergo-L repository's corpus tables (Project Gutenberg texts) and Kalamine keymaps (WTFPL v2).",
